        "title": "Video consistency and reliability: set pieces, cut audit, joins, cheap Retry",
        "type": "epic",
        "description": "Spec: docs/video-consistency-spec.md. ADR: docs/adr/0002-audited-cuts-and-set-pieces.md. From the 2026-11-14 grilling session. Follows TreeTutor-tq7 (Remotion validator fix).\n\n## Decisions so far\n\n- Manim validator checks only literal colour/font text, like the fixed Remotion validator; Manim cuts are checked when written.\n- Instructions explain the validator rules up front. Two tries per cut; the repair sees the real error with paths stripped, and doubles as the cut audit.\n- Set pieces: the plan gives each recurring object a look; one call writes shared components every Remotion cut must use.\n- One cut audit per cut, all in parallel, before the cut plays; code plus 960x540 frames per sentence end and the last frame; aligns to the plan, not the neighbour; a broken fix falls back.\n- Joins: continuing cut = hard cut; scene change = plan-chosen @remotion/transitions effect played one side at a time.\n- Pen is for emphasis only; freehand stays; visible pen tip.\n- Retry rewrites only failed cuts; errors read 'Cut N of M: reason'.",
